{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the use of simple borate esters, specifically trimethyl borate and tris(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl) borate, as effective reagents for the direct amidation of carboxylic acids and the transamidation of primary amides. The methods are characterized by high functional group tolerance, simple work-up procedures, and the ability to operate without strictly anhydrous conditions.",
